\p{For now, let #{G} be an abelian group. Given #{A, B \subseteq G}, we defined #{A \pm B = \lbrace a \pm b : a \in A,\; b \in B\rbrace }. If #{A} and #{B} are finite, then}

##{\max\lbrace |A|, |B|\rbrace  \leq |A \pm B| \leq |A||B|}

\p{(and better bounds are available in certain settings).}

