\p{Observe that if #{G} is finite, then}

##{|A|^3E(A, A) = |G|^3 \cdot \mathbb{E}_{x + y = z + w}\mathbf{1}_A(x)\mathbf{1}_A(y)\mathbf{1}_A(z)\mathbf{1}_A(w) = |G|^3\Vert \widehat{\mathbf{1}_A}\Vert _4^4}

\p{by Example sheet 1, Question 3.}

\transclude{AC1C}

\transclude{AC1D}

\transclude{AC1E}

\p{In particular, if #{A \subseteq G} is such that #{|A + A| \leq K|A|}, then #{E(A, A) \geq \frac{1}{K} > 0}. The converse is \em{not} true.}

